Imported folders: src/main/cpp/rendering/vulkan as rendering/vulkan, with cull, device, frame, layout, presentation, raster, selection, sort and world.
Also imported: src/main/cpp/engine/TraceSection.h as engine/TraceSection.h, src/main/cpp/cmake as cmake, and tests as tests.
Left out: raster/splat.vert, the CPU-order path, the rest of src/main/cpp engine, jni, src/main/cpp/splatkit.map, Kotlin with its src/test tests, resources, src/main/AndroidManifest.xml, consumer-rules.pro, README.md, docs and Gradle.
Field Guide keeps its own sfg_vulkan and CMakeLists.txt, which also builds tests with SPLATKIT_ANDROID_BUILD_TESTS.
Dependencies: vk-bootstrap v1.4.307, VulkanMemoryAllocator v3.2.1.
Dependency notices: licenses/, also bundled in the Android APK.
Field Guide patches:
- rendering/vulkan/guide: Field Guide's own, the label stream and GuideUniform bindings (10 and 11 of the visibility set) and guide_style.glsl.
- layout/splat_projection.glsl and cull/visibility.comp: each splat reads its label, the reveal clips it, its style's opacity scales alpha before the cutoff and radius, and its style and the reveal glow tint its colour.
- cull/VulkanVisibilityPass: Input takes the label stream and the guide uniform, validates and binds them, and the capability check counts them.
- frame/VulkanFrameCompute: encode takes the world's labels and writes one GuideUniform per frame slot from the frame's styles and reveal.
- world/VulkanWorld: each world and slab owns a label stream of at least 16 bytes, written by upload and uploadTile.
- raster/VulkanSplatPipeline: the CPU-order pipeline, bindWorld and draw are removed, since splat.vert is left out.
- VulkanSplatRenderer: failed() latches device, frame, encode and surface failures and visibility status; an endFrame error returns false; no CPU-order draw; black clear.
- presentation/VulkanFrameLoop.h: failed() exposes the completion failure.
- presentation/VulkanSurface.cpp: resize sets the TextureView producer's buffer size before the rebuild.
- tests: CMakeLists.txt comment; WorldFrameCompletionTest drops upstream's JNI event ordinals; VulkanSplatPipelineTest drops the CPU-order cases; the visibility, frame compute and world tests add the label stream and guide cases.
